<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gusinje</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gusinje is a small town in eastern Montenegro, close to the Albanian border in the Prokletije mountains. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a> awarded it and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plav">Plav</a> to Montenegro in 1878, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a> of the League of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prizren">Prizren</a> fought to keep them, and the great powers gave Montenegro the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulcinj">Ulcinj</a> instead in 1880. Montenegro gained Gusinje in 1912.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gusinje.jpg" alt="Gusinje" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin Brož · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gusinje,_typicke_mestske_domy_z_pocatku_19._stol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
